          text:
              'At the school gate, Sheikh Uncle was standing outside his small bookshop beside the school. Rashid greeted him, “Assalam o Alaikum, Sheikh Uncle.” “Wa Alaikum Assalam,” Sheikh Uncle replied warmly. He had overheard enough of the boys’ conversation to understand what Hamid was considering. “Wanting to lead is not wrong,” he told Hamid. “But leadership is service, not a shortcut to importance. If you want people to respect you, begin by respecting their freedom to choose.” Hamid looked away. “I just want to win.” “Then win in a way you will still be proud of after the cheering stops,” Sheikh Uncle replied. As the boys moved on, Rashid noticed a small folded note near the gate. In neat handwriting it read: “The best thing you can leave behind is a good memory.” In the lower corner was one tiny dot of green ink. Rashid looked up and down the road, but whoever had left it was gone.',
