          end: Duration(milliseconds: 333479),
          text:
              'At the end of the week, Miss held an anonymous practice poll to see how the class was thinking. "This is not the final election," she reminded them. "Choose a Captain for trust, responsibility and respect – not because of gifts or impossible promises." The practice count was twenty-two for Hamid, six for Rashid and four undecided. Hamid threw his hands into the air as if he had won a cricket match. Rashid did not look embarrassed, but he did look thoughtful. The number six stayed with him.',
