          end: Duration(milliseconds: 371693),
          text:
              'He wondered what the writer had really meant. Perhaps it was not about leaving behind something big or important. Maybe it was about the small things people remembered, like the way you helped someone, the way you spoke to them, or the way you made them feel respected. Rashid thought about his entire life at school, the way he had helped other children, even when nobody had thanked him. Maybe those moments were not wasted after all. He felt that being a good person was not always about winning votes or getting praised.',
